From: richie-rich90454 <rjiang880@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0004/0014] Remove all telemetry

This patch pins telemetry off in product.json. The OSS tree ships no
telemetry keys or endpoints: the workbench telemetry service stays a
no-op without product aiConfig, the TAS assignment service never
fetches without product tasConfig, and settings sync has no store
without product configurationSyncStore. The explicit flag makes the
posture auditable and survives any future key injection.

Residual, accepted: webview bootstrap scripts load from the static
vscode-cdn.net asset host when the server does not set a webview
endpoint. That fetch carries no workspace data and is outside the
no-network blocklist; serving those assets locally is future work.

Rationale: VS Code ships Azure Application Insights telemetry to
Microsoft. A self-hosted IDE must not send data outside the workspace.

Touches:
  - product.json (enableTelemetry)

Verification: ide/tests/no-network-test/ asserts no outbound connections.

---
diff --git a/product.json b/product.json
index b62894b..89f3d83 100644
--- a/product.json
+++ b/product.json
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 	"licenseName": "MIT",
 	"licenseUrl": "https://github.com/example/jahaziel/blob/main/LICENSE",
 	"quality": "stable",
+	"enableTelemetry": false,
 	"serverLicenseUrl": "https://github.com/example/jahaziel/blob/main/LICENSE",
 	"serverGreeting": [],
 	"serverLicense": [],
